{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib; s=pathlib.Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream\\\").read_text().splitlines()[14];print(s[:1300]);print(s[-700:])'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a\ndata.\\n   117\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   118\\t    final band there.\\n   119\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   120\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   121\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   126\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   127\\t- Other open defects.\\n   128\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   129\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib,difflib; p=pathlib.Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers\\\"); s=json.loads((p/\\\"codex-r72c.stream\\\").read_text().splitlines()[14])[\\\"item\\\"][\\\"aggregated_output\\\"]; a=[l.split(\\\"\\\\t\\\",1)[1] for l in s.splitlines()]; b=(p/\\\"FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\\\").read_text().splitlines();print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(difflib.unified_diff(a,b,n=0)))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib,difflib; p=pathlib.Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers\\\"); s=json.loads((p/\\\"codex-r72c.stream\\\").read_text().splitlines()[14])[\\\"item\\\"][\\\"aggregated_output\\\"]; a=[l.split(\\\"\\\\t\\\",1)[1] for l in s.splitlines()]; b=(p/\\\"FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\\\").read_text().splitlines();print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(difflib.unified_diff(a,b,n=0)))'\"","aggregated_output":"--- \n\n+++ \n\n@@ -10 +10 @@\n\n-**Revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\n+**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\n@@ -36,0 +37,3 @@\n\n+- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\n+  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\n+  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\n@@ -82 +85,5 @@\n\n-## 4. Yes/No questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n+**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\n+binary event such as \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\n+every question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\n+\n+## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n@@ -91,2 +98,9 @@\n\n-- **Claude's lean is (b).** It keeps value and is decided by structure. It needs a $0 census of how many Yes/No judgements it keeps\n-  on the stored stores before release.\n+- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\n+  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\n+  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\n+  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\n+- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\n+  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\n+  `why_changed`.\n+- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\n+  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\n@@ -114,0 +129,5 @@\n\n+- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\n+  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with no scored driver and no\n+    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\n+  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\n+    prose rule.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"1. Revision 4 adds the package boundary and acceptance case that 72c requested. The builder must call the exporter directly, and the check covers the finished package. The `old-1/v8` idea card must show its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” with no scored driver or substitute band. The same package must preserve both event labels and omit their spending forecasts. I found no unrelated change. [Revision 3 snapshot:15](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:15) · [Design:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:37) · [Design:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:129)\n2. One prose rule now covers events and Yes/No questions, including all 85 overlapping cases. The figures match 72c. Option (b) would preserve explanations for 21 of 85 latest answers and 73 of 73 historical answers in the sealed ledger. The design recommends (a) to Alex. Under (a), I found no remaining route in the design for a stored number forecast to reach a release reader. [72c:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:5) · [Design:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Design:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:98)\n3. **One correction from 72c is incomplete.** Line 97 still tells Alex that an explanation kept under (b) “cannot quote a number forecast.” Line 102 correctly says it can. A Yes/No answer can repeat a spending forecast from its previous explanation even when the current request shows no number question directly. Delete the sentence spanning lines 96–97 that makes the guarantee. [Design:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:96) · [Design:102](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:102) · [judging.py:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:211)\n\n**Verdict — not ready as written.** The contradictory guarantee is the only blocker. Once removed, the design is ready to hand to release work when Alex opens it, with §4’s choice still his and **(a) recommended**."}}
